# WhatsApp outbound safety

## Never create a send loop

- Bot / alert bodies must start with `Vira ·` or `OK ·` (echo-guard). Never start with the command prefix `Finora ` / `finora `.
- After a successful or failed send, mark queue status with `markOutboundSent` / `markOutboundFailed` (`updateOne` `$set` status fields only). **Do not** `document.save()` on outbound after send — stale `kind` enum validation leaves `pending` and re-sends forever.
- Any new `WhatsAppOutbound.kind` value must be added to `WHATSAPP_OUTBOUND_KINDS` in `src/lib/whatsapp/outbound-kinds.ts` (schema + producers share it). Restart `finora-vira` after kind changes.
- Deduped alerts need a stable `dedupeKey`; do not enqueue duplicates as new pending rows.

## Tests required

When changing WA outbound, echo-guard, alert kinds, or `wa-vira` flush: update/run `src/lib/whatsapp/outbound-spam-guard.test.ts` and relevant `npm run test:wa-weekly` / `test:wa-fixed-cost` scripts.
